Since I've appointed myself Elephant evangelist, I have to correct this.
The Elephant is like a Wiki, but it has a strict tree structure. That way,
you can actually *find* what people have said about things: people can
only post issues ("What is the meaning of fa'a?"), positions ("The meaning
of fa'a is X") and arguments ("The meaning of fa'a should be X because
Y".) So even if there is *no* final consensus, there is still a document
of record people can easily peruse.

